environment meets all growth requirements, mold releases spores and volatile organic compounds into the air which once inhaled makes the individual fall sick. Mold spores can find their way into the human body through the skin or when breathed in. in the same vein, food is not exempted. You can also get exposed to mold through rotten food.\nWhere are the most vulnerable spots for mold growth indoors? Mold spores are everywhere. They are in our homes, offices, educational institutions, and banks, you name it. While mold spores come into the home through air, others may be attached to your cloth, bags, or even pet’s fur. Your air conditioning unit can also bring in mold.\nThere are different types of indoor mold, amongst which black mold is considered one of the deadliest. Black mold, when breathed in, causes a wide range of health issues. Common areas to find mold in the home include bathroom, kitchen, damp cabinets, basement, potted plants, washing machines, air conditioning unit, drywall, and many more. You should also be mindful of personal items such as sponges, lunchboxes, and more.\nWhere can you find mold in the outdoors? Here are some of the surfaces where you risk exposure to mold – beaches, backyards, sidewalks, playgrounds, and forests. You’ll find mold in damp woods, piles of wet leaves, and rotted tree back.\nMold can also be found on food such as bread, nuts, and cereal. These molds release harmful toxins known as mycotoxins. Ingesting food infested with mold can cause serious health complications such as weakened immune systems, acute poisoning, cancer, and in extreme cases death.\nRisks Associated with Exposure to Mold\nProlonged mold exposure isn’t advised. It can cause immune deficiencies which make you vulnerable to getting infected by just about any virus or bacteria. However, some people are more sensitive to mold than others. Those suffering from allergies might experience health complications when exposed to mold. Symptoms may include one or more of the following: cough, cold, fever, skin irritation, and difficulty in breathing.\nMold remediation services Maine has been in the business of protecting homes from mold attacks. Hire these professionals and e","tokens":["M","olds"," can"," live"," anywhere",","," indoors"," and"," outdoors","."," There"," are"," millions"," of"," mold"," species","."," While"," it"," is"," regarded"," as"," harmful"," to"," human"," health",","," it"," is"," quite"," useful"," for"," the"," planet","’","s"," ecosystem","."," How"," is"," this"," so","?"," Mold"," is"," a"," fungus"," that"," helps"," waste"," products"," break"," down","."," Some"," people"," who"," get"," exposed"," to"," mold"," growth"," develop"," symptoms","."," Others"," have"," no"," symptoms"," and"," do"," not"," fall"," sick","."," Mold"," remed","iation"," services"," Maine"," can"," help"," prevent"," you"," and"," your"," family"," from"," getting"," sick"," due"," to"," mold"," exposure"," in"," the"," home","."," It"," is"," advis","able"," that"," you"," reach"," out"," to"," mold"," experts"," immediately"," you"," discover"," mold"," signs"," in"," the"," home","."," Otherwise",","," you"," risk"," exp","ending"," more"," travel"," time"," to"," the"," physician","’","s"," office"," due"," to"," mold"," exposure",".","\n","How"," Do"," We"," Come"," In"," Contact"," With"," Mold","?","\n","M","old"," can","’","t"," survive"," without"," food","."," They"," thrive"," on"," moisture"," and"," organic"," matter","."," If"," an"," environment"," meets"," all"," growth"," requirements",","," mold"," releases"," spores"," and"," volatile"," organic"," compounds"," into"," the"," air"," which"," once"," inhaled"," makes"," the"," individual"," fall"," sick","."," Mold"," spores"," can"," find"," their"," way"," into"," the"," human"," body"," through"," the"," skin"," or"," when"," breathed"," in","."," in"," the"," same"," vein",","," food"," is"," not"," exempt","ed","."," You"," can"," also"," ge